    Final;1;552;;0,0,0,1;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.CommentaryNode, AmplifyShaderEditor,
    Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;535;-1104,6720;Inherit;False;759.5498;410.8044;;6;585;584;583;582;581;580;;0,0,0,1;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.CommentaryNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;536;-320,6848;Inherit;False;366.8999;226.9;Derivative
    DDX DDY;4;626;625;578;577;;0,0,0,1;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.CommentaryNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;537;2176,8480;Inherit;False;127.2;126.7999;UV
    DDY;1;548;;0,0,0,1;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.CommentaryNode, AmplifyShaderEditor,
    Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;538;2176,8336;Inherit;False;125.6;129.9998;UV
    DDX;1;549;;0,0,0,1;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode, AmplifyShaderEditor,
    Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;271;688,2592;Inherit;False;439.5477;106.7559;;;0,0,0,1;We
    want to move the UV coordinates away in the view direction, so we start with
    the view direction in Tangent Space and multiply that by the height map data.;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;277;-224,2816;Inherit;False;424.1;122.8;;;0,0,0,1;The
    heightmap is a black and white image that defines the depth of the texture. Tall
    areas are white and low areas are black. Gradient images without hard edges between
    black and white work best.;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode, AmplifyShaderEditor,
    Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;278;-816,2016;Inherit;False;519.5023;208.8508;;;0,0,0,1;The
    Parallax Mapping Node creates UV coordinates used to sample a texture.  The UVs
    have been altered per pixel such that they create the illusion that the sampled
    texture has thickness or depth rather than just being flat.$$This illusion is
    most visible when moving the camera around.$$This is effect is only slightly
    more expensive than plain normal mapping.  It's doing one extra texture sample
    for the height map and a little bit of extra math, but it's still considered
    pretty cheap.$$$;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode, AmplifyShaderEditor,
    Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;283;864,3232;Inherit;False;296.8999;176.8;;;0,0,0,1;Amplitude
    controls the maximum height range of the effect. Values that are too high tend
    to pull the effect apart and break the illusion.  Values that are too low aren't
    visible, so finding the right balance is important.;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;298;1392,2816;Inherit;False;268.8818;135.25;;;0,0,0,1;The
    resulting UVs are shifted away from the viewer in the view direciton when the
    height map is white.;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode, AmplifyShaderEditor,
    Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;376;-592,2832;Inherit;False;266;102;Enable
    Custom Derivative;;0,0,0,1;Useful for optimization when daisy chaining Parallax
    Mapping ;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.WireNode, AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0,
    Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;384;-256,4560;Inherit;False;1;0;FLOAT2;0,0;False;1;FLOAT2;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.WireNode,
