    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;435;768,4624;Inherit;False;FLOAT3;0;1;2;3;1;0;FLOAT2;0,0;False;1;FLOAT3;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;439;-1680,1968;Inherit;False;524.6;346.3;Parallax
    Nodes;;0,0,0,1;$$Parallax Occlusion$Parallax occlusion mapping (POM) provides
    Height Scale and adjustable reference plan for height starting point $$Parallax
    Iteration Normal$Cheaper less quality than POM,  Artifacts are based view angle$$Parallax
    Iteration Planar$More accurate than Iteration Normal, may have more artifacts
    on steep angles  $$Parallax BiDirectional$similar to occlusion mapping with added
    ability to define number of iterations$$;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.TextureCoordinatesNode,
